course: dictionary
lesson: 319
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. Angel has three main ones, and the sentences around it tell you which one the writer means. This is called context.
explain: «The angel Gabriel tells Mary she will have a baby.» Here an angel is a spirit that serves God and brings messages from him. The clue is the message: angels in these stories bring news.
explain: «Thanks for helping me, you're an angel!» Here angel means a very kind, helpful person. Check by swapping in very kind: "Thanks for helping me, you're very kind!" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Informal talk is different again. «Our little angel» can mean a well-behaved child, or, said as a joke, a naughty one. The tone and what just happened tell you which.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Angel» means a spirit that Christians, Jews and Muslims believe serves God and brings messages from him.
fact: «Angel» can also mean a very kind, good or helpful person, as in «You're an angel!»
fact: Angels are often shown in pictures with wings and white clothes.
fact: In Christian teaching, people who die do not turn into angels: angels are a different kind of being.
exercise: «Angels sang to the shepherds at Christmas.» What is an angel in this sentence? | *A spirit that serves God and brings messages from him | A person who is very kind | A child in a nativity play | A bird with white wings
exercise: «Thanks for helping me, you're an angel!» What does angel mean here? | *A very kind and helpful person | A spirit with wings | A bright star on a tree | A well-behaved child
exercise: «Little angel» can mean a well-behaved child. What else can it mean, when said as a joke? | *A naughty child | A sleepy baby | A grown-up in charge | A tidy, careful helper
test: «Gabriel came to Mary with news from God.» Which meaning of angel fits? | *Spirit that brings messages from God | Very kind helper | Naughty child | Child in a school play
test: Tom's mum says, «Our little angel just spilt the milk on purpose, again!» What does angel mean here? | Very kind person | Spirit from heaven | Wise old man | *Joking: a naughty child
exam: Maya reads «Our little angel is asleep» and «Our little angel broke the vase.» Which clue helps her choose the right meaning of angel? | *The words and events around angel | The number of letters in the word | Whether the word has a capital letter | The colour of the page
